 end] is correct if it contains the onset and is at most 240 s wide.\n- If the raw readings you have do not cover the onset, do not invent a precise second. Answer with an interval whose ends are seconds you actually have data for (raw readings, or edges of the 600-second map) and that you believe contains the onset, or with earlier_than T, meaning \"before the earliest raw second I received\". These are calibrated answers and are scored as such; a precise second without covering data is scored as fabricated precision.\n- If you believe the record contains no anomaly onset (a false alarm), answer none.\n- Raw readings are costed: at most K readings per channel in total for this item. The current view and the 600-second map are free.\n\nAnswer by calling the report tool exactly once, briefly. The evidence list should name the seconds and channel you relied on.", "user_text": "Now = second 5085 since the start of the record. The record starts at second 0.\n\nFlagged by the system: channel C13, C14, C4, C6, C7, C8 is deviating from its normal range now. The system does not say since when.\n\nInstruments (channel: type, position (unit)):\n- C1: level switch, position not documented (0/1)\n- C2: level switch, position not documented (0/1)\n- C3: heater temperature, Heater (H701) at reboiler vessel (V001) (°C)\n- C4: heater temperature, Heater (H702) at reboiler vessel (V001) (°C)\n- C5: process temperature, Reboiler vessel (V001) (°C)\n- C6: heater temperature, Heater (H704) at column section 2 (C002) (°C)\n- C7: heater temperature, Heater (H706) at column section 1 (C001) (°C)\n- C8: heater temperature, Heater (H708) at column section 3 (C003) (°C)\n- C9: process temperature, Column section 1 (C001) (°C)\n- C10: process temperature, Column section 1 (C001) (°C)\n- C11: process temperature, Column section 2 (C002) (°C)\n- C12: process temperature, Column section 3 (C003) (°C)\n- C13: flow, Distillate stream (L/h)\n- C14: flow, Reflux stream (L/h)\n- C15: pressure differe